systools is a set of small command-line tools, written in POSIX sh and
behaving the same on FreeBSD and Linux: ZFS snapshot rotation, the
default gateway, a laptop's dock, VPN tunnel status for a status bar,
the place a machine is at from its Wi-Fi, X11 screen layout, screenshots,
PDF shrinking and rasterising, QR codes, Pushover notifications, speech
synthesis and transcription, Mullvad relay selection, and more. Each
tool needs only what its own job is about, and has a manual page.

The DAV option adds caldav and carddav, CalDAV and CardDAV clients
written in Ruby.
